.TH QUADCAPD 1 "2026" "quadcap" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quadcapd \- inspect and control an Elgato 4K60 Pro MK.2 from the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadcapd
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B quadcapd
reports what the capture card sees and records from it without opening a
window. It is the way to check a signal over SSH, and the way to script a
capture.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-status
Print the card, the device node, and the signal currently locked.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Keep printing as the signal changes.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit the status as JSON rather than text.
.TP
.B \-\-get\-edid
Write the EDID the card presents to the console to standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-set\-edid " " \fIFILE\fR
Load an EDID into the card. The MK.2 holds this in its MCU, so it is lost on
a power cycle and has to be written again at boot.
.TP
.B \-\-edid\-source " " \fISOURCE\fR
Choose whether the card presents its internal EDID, the attached display's, or
a merge of the two.
.TP
.B \-\-setup
Report whether the driver is installed, loaded, and signed.
.TP
.B \-\-record " " \fIFILE\fR
Record to \fIFILE\fR. Combine with \fB\-\-seconds\fR, \fB\-\-width\fR,
\fB\-\-height\fR, \fB\-\-fps\fR, and \fB\-\-software\fR.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadcap (1)
